========================================
ATTRIBUTES (Non-Programming Explanation)
========================================

DEFINITION
----------
An attribute is a quality, feature, or characteristic
that describes something.

It tells you:
- What it is like
- What it has
- What makes it different


PERSON EXAMPLE
--------------
A person can have attributes such as:

- Hair color
- Height
- Age
- Kindness
- Sense of humor

Example:
Maria has brown hair, is 5'6", and is very patient.

Hair color, height, and patience are attributes.


OBJECT EXAMPLE (Car)
--------------------
A car can have attributes such as:

- Color
- Brand
- Speed
- Fuel type
- Number of doors

Example:
A red, electric, four-door car.

Red, electric, and four-door are attributes.


PLACE EXAMPLE (House)
---------------------
A house can have attributes such as:

- Size
- Location
- Number of rooms
- Age
- Style

Example:
A large, modern house with 3 bedrooms.

Large, modern, and 3 bedrooms are attributes.


HOW TO RECOGNIZE AN ATTRIBUTE
-----------------------------
If you can say:

- "It has..."
- "It is..."
- "It looks..."

You are probably describing an attribute.


ONE-SENTENCE SUMMARY
--------------------
An attribute is a detail that helps describe what something is like.

========================================
PARAMETERS (Non-Programming Explanation)
========================================

DEFINITION
----------
A parameter is a limit, rule, condition, or input
that controls how something works or what is allowed.

It tells you:
- What can change
- What is allowed
- What the boundaries are


PERSON EXAMPLE
--------------
A person might have parameters such as:

- Must be 18 years old to vote
- Must arrive by 9:00 AM
- Budget limit of $50
- Only 2 guests allowed

Example:
Maria can attend the event only if she arrives before 9:00 PM.

The time requirement is a parameter.


OBJECT EXAMPLE (Car)
--------------------
A car can have parameters such as:

- Maximum speed limit of 120 mph
- Fuel capacity of 15 gallons
- Tire pressure range (30–35 PSI)
- Weight limit of 5 passengers

Example:
The car can carry up to 5 people.

The passenger limit is a parameter.


PLACE EXAMPLE (House)
---------------------
A house can have parameters such as:

- Rent must be paid by the 5th
- Maximum 4 occupants
- No pets allowed
- Quiet hours after 10 PM

Example:
Only 4 people can live in the house.

The occupancy limit is a parameter.


HOW TO RECOGNIZE A PARAMETER
----------------------------
If you can say:

- "It must..."
- "It can only..."
- "Up to..."
- "Between X and Y..."

You are probably describing a parameter.


ONE-SENTENCE SUMMARY
--------------------
A parameter is a rule, limit, or condition that controls what is allowed or how something works.

====================================================
ATTRIBUTES vs PARAMETERS (Simple Comparison)
====================================================

WHAT THEY ARE
-------------
Attribute  = A characteristic or feature that describes something.
Parameter  = A rule, limit, or condition that controls something.


WHAT THEY ANSWER
----------------
Attribute  = "What is it like?"
Parameter  = "What are the limits or conditions?"


KEY WORD CLUES
--------------
Attribute  = It is..., It has..., It looks...
Parameter  = It must..., It can only..., Up to..., Between...


PERSON EXAMPLE
--------------
Attribute  = Brown hair, 5'6", patient
Parameter  = Must be 18 to vote, must arrive by 9 PM


CAR EXAMPLE
-----------
Attribute  = Red, electric, four-door
Parameter  = Max speed 120 mph, up to 5 passengers


HOUSE EXAMPLE
-------------
Attribute  = Large, modern, 3 bedrooms
Parameter  = Maximum 4 occupants, no pets allowed


MAIN DIFFERENCE
---------------
Attributes describe.
Parameters control.


ONE-LINE MEMORY TRICK
---------------------
Attributes = Qualities.
Parameters = Limits.



