                 PROPERTY vs ATTRIBUTE — COMPLETE MASTER NOTE
===============================================================================

DEFINITION (GENERAL ENGLISH)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Property  = A quality/feature of something OR something owned
Attribute = A characteristic that describes something

Example:

DOG
 |
 |-- Color = Brown
 |-- Age = 3
 |-- Breed = Labrador

Color, Age, Breed
→ can be called properties
→ can also be called attributes

In everyday English:
Property ≈ Attribute


OWNERSHIP MEANING
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Property can also mean something you legally own.

Examples:
- House
- Land
- Building

Example:
A house in New York City
→ That house is your property.


IN PROGRAMMING
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

PROPERTY (Object-Oriented Programming)

Property = Data stored inside an object

Think of an object as a digital thing.

Example:

Car Object
 |
 |-- color = "Red"
 |-- speed = 120
 |-- brand = "Toyota"

color, speed, brand
→ are properties of the Car object

In OOP languages like Java, Python, and C#,
object data members are usually called properties.

Example structure:

Person
 |
 |-- name
 |-- age

name and age → properties


ATTRIBUTE (Programming Contexts)

1) HTML (Web Development)

Attribute = Extra information added to something

Example concept:

Image element
 |
 |-- src
 |-- width

src and width → attributes

Rule:
Element → has attributes


2) DATABASES

User Table
 |
 |-- name
 |-- email
 |-- age

Each column can be called:
→ Attribute

Rule:
Table column = Attribute


SIMPLE PROGRAMMING DIFFERENCE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Property  = Data inside an object (OOP)
Attribute = Descriptive data (HTML or Database)

BUT in real-world usage:
Property ≈ Attribute
(often used interchangeably)


FINAL BEGINNER RULE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
If talking about objects → say PROPERTY
If talking about HTML or databases → say ATTRIBUTE

Do not overthink it.
Even experienced programmers sometimes mix the terms.

Property = A characteristic OR something owned
Object → stores data → that data is a property
